# Emergency AI helper
# 1. Copy this file and name the copy .env (same folder). .env is git-ignored, so your keys never get committed.
# 2. Paste a key after the = sign. No quotes, no spaces. One key is enough; with both, Claude is tried first
#    and Gemini is the backup when Claude fails or is slow.
# 3. Run: npm run dev
# Keys are only read by the local dev server / Vercel function, never sent to the browser.

# Claude (Anthropic Console: console.anthropic.com)
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# Gemini (Google AI Studio)
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-3.8-flash
# GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODELS=gemini-3.7-flash,gemini-3.5-flash   (tried in order if the main model is busy or missing)

# Optional: other domains allowed to call the helper
# ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://your-other-domain.example
